[Expected Approach] Using Two Pointer Technique - O(n) Time and O(1) SpaceThe idea is to use two pointers, one starting at the head and the other at the end of the sorted doubly linked list. Move the first pointer forward if the sum of the two pointer's values is less than the target, or move the second pointer backward if the sum is greater. Continue until the pointers meet or cross each other.An efficient solution for this problem is the same as Pair with given Sum (Two Sum) article.  Initialize two pointer variables to find the candidate elements in the sorted doubly linked list. Initialize first with the start of the doubly linked list and second with the last node.If current sum of first and second is less than x, then we move first in forward direction. If current sum of first and second element is greater than x, then we move second in backward direction.The loop terminates when two pointers cross each other (second->next = first), or they become the same (first == second).
